      "content": "Embracing the stillness and his acceptance can be the most devastatingly honest path for your character. If he accepts the stillness, the scene shouldn't be dramatic, but deeply internal and observational. Focus on the texture of that letting go—the cessation of internal fighting, not the action itself. This powerful surrender, written with unflinching realism, will resonate far more deeply than any forced spark of hope.",
